nodecode-xai-collections is a rewrite of Julientalbot's Julientalbot/hermes-xai:

  https://github.com/Julientalbot/hermes-xai
  commit 8fd9bf8ecef1f8e9cb2cb7921fc86527acd9ede3
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Julien Talbot (LICENSE)

The rewritten part is that plugin's collections module: the
xai_collections_search tool in __init__.py, with its name, its description
and its five parameters, over hermes_xai/collections_search.py. The two REST
calls are the original's and go to the same origin — GET
https://api.x.ai/v1/collections and POST https://api.x.ai/v1/documents/search
with Authorization: Bearer <key> — as are its behaviour and limits: the
collection_<uuid> shape a passed id must have, a default of 5 passages and a
cap of 20, the 2000-character clip on each passage, the fallback from the
call's ids to the section's default ids to every collection of the team
(asking the listing first), a passage's title read from fields.title and
falling back to its file_id, and an empty query or a badly shaped id refused
before any request is made. The key is read from the profile's environment
(the original reads it through the host's secret scope) and is sent only to
api.x.ai.

What was left out, and why: the plugin's other half, the Grok Voice module
(hermes_xai/voice.py, dashboard/plugin_api.py and desktop/plugin.js), is a
full-duplex WebSocket call driven by a button in Hermes Desktop's composer,
minting a 300-second client secret from the backend and streaming microphone
audio to wss://api.x.ai/v1/realtime. That is a desktop window and a realtime
transport, not a wire a tool cell can carry, so the cell serves the tool and
a /collections command instead of the voice button. The plugin's own install
path and settings page are replaced by the cell's config section and
/settings.

LICENSE is the original repository's LICENSE, unchanged.
